00:25:35.441 --> 00:25:40.030
So, basically, the approach
in Batson, Spielman,

00:25:40.031 --> 00:25:42.080
Srivastava, is they are going to

00:25:42.081 --> 00:25:46.580
maintain the current sum of
these rank-one matrices.

00:25:46.581 --> 00:25:51.020
They're going to start with
A equal to zero and two

00:25:51.021 --> 00:25:55.950
barrier values that basically
sandwich this PSD matrix A.

00:25:55.951 --> 00:25:59.365
So, initially, l would be minus,

00:25:59.366 --> 00:26:01.360
minus something, or
minus a quarter or

00:26:01.361 --> 00:26:03.270
something and u
would be a quarter.

00:26:03.271 --> 00:26:06.575
So, basically, in
the very beginning,

00:26:06.576 --> 00:26:10.525
it's a zero matrix
sandwich Pi minus i and i.

00:26:10.526 --> 00:26:15.200
The algorithm will try to
add edge iteratively and

00:26:15.201 --> 00:26:19.440
deterministically every time
to grow this ellipsoid,

00:26:19.441 --> 00:26:22.885
while keeping it away from
the lower and upper barrier.

00:26:22.886 --> 00:26:25.355
Okay? The important
thing for us here,

00:26:25.356 --> 00:26:27.765
is the only thing you need to
know about this algorithm,

00:26:27.766 --> 00:26:29.455
is they actually add edge

00:26:29.456 --> 00:26:31.685
deterministically
in each iteration.

00:26:31.686 --> 00:26:34.270
Why they are able to
show that it works?

00:26:34.271 --> 00:26:37.145
Is they can say that a
good edge always exists,

00:26:37.146 --> 00:26:39.860
because you can take
an average edge.

00:26:39.861 --> 00:26:42.295
So, remember, in their problem

00:26:42.296 --> 00:26:44.095
all the vector sum up to i.

00:26:44.096 --> 00:26:45.420
Which means if you take

00:26:45.421 --> 00:26:47.960
a tiny fraction of
an average edge.

00:26:47.961 --> 00:26:49.250
So, basically, you
take a tiny fraction

00:26:49.251 --> 00:26:50.600
of every edge then,

00:26:50.601 --> 00:26:52.184
your ball, then, you're ellipsoid

00:26:52.185 --> 00:26:54.725
would just grow by identity.

00:26:54.726 --> 00:26:57.380
So you know that
one vector is going to

00:26:57.381 --> 00:27:00.205
help you in the right potential
function that you define.

00:27:00.206 --> 00:27:04.675
So, basically, you're going
to start with- basically,

00:27:04.676 --> 00:27:07.310
the hope is the difference

00:27:07.311 --> 00:27:10.480
between the two variables
are going to stay the same,

00:27:10.481 --> 00:27:12.540
but the barriers would events

00:27:12.541 --> 00:27:14.470
at roughly the same rate
and grow larger,

00:27:14.471 --> 00:27:16.220
and larger, and this ellipsoid

00:27:16.221 --> 00:27:18.310
will become more and
more like a sphere.

00:27:18.311 --> 00:27:22.430
That's the idea behind the BSS.

00:27:23.910 --> 00:27:27.920
Good. I want to talk about
this deterministically part.

00:27:27.921 --> 00:27:30.130
So, basically, the algorithm can

00:27:30.131 --> 00:27:32.645
